{"id":"h6-08-p8","title":"Design a web crawler","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: requirements, API, estimates, URL frontier, politeness, dedupe, traps, recrawl. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","html":"<p><strong>A web crawler starts from a few seed URLs, downloads pages, extracts the links in them, and keeps going so that the pages can be indexed.</strong> Googlebot, Bingbot, Common Crawl and the crawlers behind price-comparison sites do this. The product is simple; the difficulty is doing billions of pages politely, without repeats and without getting trapped.</p>\n<p><strong>Functional requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Given seeds, discover and fetch pages continuously.</li>\n<li>Extract text and outgoing links; store raw HTML for indexing.</li>\n<li>Do not crawl the same URL twice (dedupe URLs) or store the same content twice (dedupe content).</li>\n<li>Obey <code>robots.txt</code> and per-host rate limits (politeness).</li>\n<li>Re-crawl pages periodically; recrawl news sites more often than static ones.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Non-functional requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Throughput: 1 billion pages per month (about 400 pages/s average).</li>\n<li>Robust: survive slow, broken, huge or malicious pages and crawler traps.</li>\n<li>Extensible: later add image, PDF or JS-rendered pages.</li>\n<li>Horizontally scalable and restartable without losing progress.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 864.4 130\" width=\"864.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The crawl loop at its simplest\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L596 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L596 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M706.4 34 L762.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M706.4 34 L762.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M540 65 L596 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M540 65 L596 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M540 65 L596 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M540 65 L596 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Seed URLs</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Parser</text><rect x=\"596\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"651.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">URL frontier</text><rect x=\"596\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"651.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Page store</text><rect x=\"762.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"807.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Fetcher</text></svg><figcaption>The crawl loop at its simplest</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choose breadth-first with priorities rather than pure depth-first. Depth-first dives into one site forever (and into traps). The frontier design is the heart of the system and is a one-way-ish door: once billions of URLs sit in it, changing its structure means a migration.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A librarian walking through a city of libraries: she notes which libraries are mentioned in each book, queues them, and never visits the same one twice in a day.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not mentioning politeness and robots.txt (the first thing a real operator would ask).</li>\n<li>Ignoring crawler traps (infinite calendars, session IDs in URLs).</li>\n<li>Designing a single-machine queue for a billion-URL problem.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"api","title":"API","html":"<p>A crawler is mostly internal, but it has three surfaces: a control API, the fetch contract, and the output feed.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">POST /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/crawl/seeds</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"urls\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"https://news.example.com/\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">], </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"priority\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"high\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"recrawlEveryHours\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">202</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"batchId\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"b_55\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"accepted\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/crawl/status?host=news.example.com</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"host\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"news.example.com\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"queued\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">18400</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"fetched24h\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">91233</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">      \"errorRate\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0.012</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"crawlDelayMs\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1000</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"robotsFetchedAt\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"2026-11-09T06:00:00Z\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Internal worker contract (gRPC or message): the frontier hands a <strong>lease</strong>, the fetcher returns a result.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// frontier -> fetcher (lease, 60 s)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"url\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"https://news.example.com/a?id=7\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"host\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"news.example.com\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"leaseId\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"l_91\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"depth\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// fetcher -> parser topic</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"url\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"...\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"status\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"contentHash\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"9c1f...\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"blobKey\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"s3://crawl/2026/11/09/9c1f.html.gz\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"fetchedAt\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"...\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"etag\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"W/</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">abc</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\\\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Output: parsed documents published to a Kafka topic <code>crawl.pages</code> for the search indexer.</p>\n<p>Politeness is part of the contract: send a clear <code>User-Agent: ExampleBot/1.0 (+https://example.com/bot)</code>, honour <code>Crawl-delay</code> and use conditional GET (<code>If-None-Match</code>, <code>If-Modified-Since</code>) on recrawl; a <code>304 Not Modified</code> saves bandwidth.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry example.</strong> Common Crawl publishes monthly dumps (WARC files on S3); Googlebot identifies itself and obeys robots.txt.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A courier job card: leased for 60 s, returned with proof of delivery or it goes back in the queue.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fetch results without leases, so a crashed worker loses URLs forever.</li>\n<li>Forgetting conditional GET on recrawl.</li>\n<li>No identifying User-Agent (gets blocked).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"estimates","title":"Estimates","html":"<p>Assume 1B pages/month, average page 500 KB raw (about 100 KB gzipped), 10 links per page after dedupe.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Calculation</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Fetch rate</td>\n<td>1B / 2.6M s</td>\n<td>~400 pages/s average, 1,000/s peak target</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bandwidth</td>\n<td>400 x 500 KB</td>\n<td>~200 MB/s = 1.6 Gbit/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Raw storage / month</td>\n<td>1B x 100 KB gzipped</td>\n<td>~100 TB / month, ~1.2 PB / year</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>URLs seen</td>\n<td>1B pages x 10 links, but heavy overlap; assume 5B unique</td>\n<td>5B URLs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>URL seen-set</td>\n<td>5B x 8 B hash</td>\n<td>~40 GB exact; Bloom filter at 1% FP needs ~9.6 bits/key = 6 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Frontier size</td>\n<td>5B x ~100 B per URL record</td>\n<td>~500 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fetcher machines</td>\n<td>one fetcher with 500 concurrent connections, avg 1 s fetch = ~500 pages/s theoretical, 100 realistic with DNS/TLS/parsing</td>\n<td>~10-20 fetcher nodes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DNS</td>\n<td>1,000 lookups/s</td>\n<td>needs a local caching resolver</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The bottleneck is almost never CPU; it is network latency, DNS and per-host politeness (you cannot hit one host faster than 1 request per second or so).</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Common Crawl ingests several billion pages per month; Google's crawl is orders of magnitude larger.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A delivery fleet limited not by trucks but by how fast each customer's door can be answered.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimating only bandwidth and forgetting DNS and politeness limits.</li>\n<li>Storing uncompressed HTML.</li>\n<li>Believing one big machine fetches 10,000 pages/s.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"high-level-design","title":"High-level design","html":"<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 1325.6 130\" width=\"1325.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Main pipeline\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L784 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L784 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.125;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.125;0.126;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M894.4 65 L950.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M894.4 65 L950.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.625;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.625;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M1068 65 L1124 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M1068 65 L1124 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.750;0.875;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.750;0.875;0.876;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M1068 65 L1124 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M1068 65 L1124 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.750;0.875;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.750;0.875;0.876;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M728 34 L784 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M728 34 L784 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.625;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"6.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.625;0.626;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Seeds</text><rect x=\"596\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"662\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Dedupe</text><rect x=\"596\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"662\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Content indexer</text><rect x=\"784\" y=\"43\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"839.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">URL frontier</text><rect x=\"950.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"1009.1999999999999\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Fetcher fleet</text><rect x=\"1124\" y=\"12\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"1218.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Raw page store</text><rect x=\"1124\" y=\"74\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"1218.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Parser / link extractor</text></svg><figcaption>Main pipeline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 884.8 192\" width=\"884.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What the fetcher consults before each download\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 96 L782.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 96 L782.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M726.8 158 L782.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M726.8 158 L782.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">URL frontier</text><rect x=\"616.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"671.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Robots cache</text><rect x=\"616.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"671.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">DNS cache</text><rect x=\"616.4\" y=\"136\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"671.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Website</text><rect x=\"782.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"827.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Fetcher</text></svg><figcaption>What the fetcher consults before each download</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Components:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>URL frontier</strong>: priority queues (front) feeding per-host queues (back) so one host is served at most once per <code>crawl-delay</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Fetcher workers</strong>: async HTTP clients (Netty, aiohttp, Go net/http), 500 connections each, 10 s timeout, 5 MB body cap.</li>\n<li><strong>DNS cache</strong>: local Unbound or an in-process cache, TTL honoured.</li>\n<li><strong>Robots cache</strong>: robots.txt per host cached for 24 h in Redis.</li>\n<li><strong>Parser</strong>: extracts text and links, normalises URLs, strips tracking parameters.</li>\n<li><strong>URL dedupe</strong>: Bloom filter in front of an exact store (RocksDB or Redis sharded by hash).</li>\n<li><strong>Content dedupe</strong>: SimHash or MinHash of the text to detect near-duplicates; SHA-256 of the body for exact duplicates.</li>\n<li><strong>Blob store</strong>: S3/HDFS for raw HTML; metadata in Cassandra/Bigtable keyed by URL hash.</li>\n<li><strong>Scheduler for recrawl</strong>: pushes URLs back into the frontier based on change rate.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity: distributed frontier partitioned by host hash.</strong> Why: all URLs of one host land on one frontier shard and one fetcher group, so politeness is enforced locally with no cross-machine locks. Alternative: partition by URL hash, which spreads load evenly but means politeness requires a distributed lock per host. Breaks when one host is huge (a Wikipedia-sized site); then sub-split by host plus path bucket while sharing a rate limiter in Redis. Changing the partition scheme is a one-way door (requeue billions of URLs), so choose host hash up front.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity: Kafka vs custom queue for the frontier.</strong> A plain Kafka topic cannot do priorities and per-host delay well. Use Kafka for the pipeline stages after fetching, and a purpose-built frontier (Redis sorted sets or a RocksDB-backed service) for scheduling. Reversible per stage.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Mercator (the classic paper) introduced the front/back queue frontier; Apache Nutch and StormCrawler implement the same idea; Heritrix powers the Internet Archive.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Airport check-in: many queues by priority (class), then one counter per airline that serves one passenger at a time.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A single global queue with no per-host structure.</li>\n<li>Parsing in the fetcher thread, which blocks the network pipeline.</li>\n<li>Forgetting a retry and dead-letter path.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"deep-dives","title":"Deep dives","html":"<h3>The URL frontier: priority and politeness</h3>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 977.1999999999999 130\" width=\"977.1999999999999\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Front queues choose WHAT is important, back queues enforce WHEN\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.79999999999995 34 L526.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.79999999999995 34 L526.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.79999999999995 96 L526.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.79999999999995 96 L526.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M616.8 65 L672.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M616.8 65 L672.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M819.1999999999999 34 L875.1999999999999 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M819.1999999999999 34 L875.1999999999999 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M616.8 65 L672.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M616.8 65 L672.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M819.1999999999999 96 L875.1999999999999 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M819.1999999999999 96 L875.1999999999999 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">New URLs</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Prioritizer</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Front queue (high)</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Front queue (low)</text><rect x=\"526.8\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"571.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Router</text><rect x=\"672.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"746\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Back queue host A</text><rect x=\"672.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"746\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Back queue host B</text><rect x=\"875.1999999999999\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"920.1999999999999\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Fetcher</text></svg><figcaption>Front queues choose WHAT is important, back queues enforce WHEN</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Front queues rank by PageRank-like score, update frequency and freshness need. A router maps each URL to one back queue per host; a min-heap keyed by \"next allowed fetch time\" tells the fetcher which host may be hit now. With <code>crawl-delay</code> 1 s and 400 fetches/s you need at least 400 distinct hosts active at all times; the heap guarantees that. Decision: leases with 60 s timeouts so a crashed fetcher returns its URLs automatically.</p>\n<h3>Dedupe of URLs</h3>\n<p>Normalise first: lowercase host, drop fragment <code>#x</code>, sort query params, remove <code>utm_*</code>, resolve <code>../</code>, strip default ports. Then check a Bloom filter (6 GB for 5B keys at 1%); a \"no\" is definitive, a \"yes\" goes to the exact store to avoid dropping a new URL on a false positive. Alternatively accept the 1% loss for low-priority URLs. Reversible, but the Bloom filter cannot delete, so rebuild it periodically.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 766.4000000000001 68\" width=\"766.4000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"URL dedupe stages\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M136.8 34 L192.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M136.8 34 L192.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M449.20000000000005 34 L505.20000000000005 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M449.20000000000005 34 L505.20000000000005 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M608.4000000000001 34 L664.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M608.4000000000001 34 L664.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"74.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Extracted link</text><rect x=\"192.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"237.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Normalise</text><rect x=\"338.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Bloom filter</text><rect x=\"505.20000000000005\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"556.8000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Exact store</text><rect x=\"664.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"709.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Frontier</text></svg><figcaption>URL dedupe stages</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Content dedupe</h3>\n<p>Exact duplicate: store <code>SHA-256(body)</code>; skip indexing if seen. Near-duplicate (same article with a different ad): SimHash 64-bit, compare Hamming distance under 3. About 30% of the web is duplicated content, so this saves index size and ranking noise.</p>\n<h3>Crawler traps and bad pages</h3>\n<p>Infinite calendars (<code>/2026/11/10</code>, <code>/2026/11/11</code>, ...), session IDs in URLs, faceted links that explode. Defences: max URL length 2,000, max depth 15, max pages per host per day, detect repeating path segments, per-host budget by importance. Cap body size at 5 MB and time at 10 s; respect <code>Content-Type</code> allow-list.</p>\n<h3>Robots.txt and politeness</h3>\n<p>Fetch <code>/robots.txt</code> first, cache 24 h; treat 4xx as \"allow all\", 5xx as \"disallow temporarily\". Obey <code>Disallow</code> and <code>Crawl-delay</code> (Google ignores crawl-delay but many crawlers honour it). Backoff on 429/503 exponentially (1 s, 2 s, 4 s ... up to 1 h) per host.</p>\n<h3>Freshness: recrawl scheduling</h3>\n<p>Estimate each page's change rate from past crawls (changed in 3 of 5 visits = high). Recrawl news front pages every few minutes, product pages daily, archives monthly. Use <code>ETag</code>/<code>If-Modified-Since</code> to make unchanged recrawls cost a tiny 304. Sitemaps (<code>sitemap.xml</code>) give hints.</p>\n<h3>JavaScript-heavy pages</h3>\n<p>A headless browser (Chrome) renders pages but is ~10-50x costlier than a plain fetch. Route only domains flagged as client-rendered into a separate render pool. Decision is reversible per domain.</p>\n<h3>Failure handling</h3>\n<p>Fetch results go to Kafka; the parser group commits offsets after writing. At-least-once delivery plus idempotent keys (URL hash) means a retry is harmless. Dead-letter after 5 failures with the reason (DNS, TLS, timeout).</p>\n<p><strong>Production incident patterns.</strong> (1) The crawler hits one host at 100 req/s and takes it down: symptom is a wave of 503 and IP bans; metric: per-host request rate. (2) Frontier shard imbalance: one shard 10x larger because of a mega-host; monitor queue depth per shard. (3) A trap generates millions of unique URLs: seen-set growth rate per host spikes.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Googlebot's adaptive crawl rate, Common Crawl's open-source tooling, Apache Nutch on Hadoop, and Scrapy for smaller jobs.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A pollster who must not knock on the same door twice, must respect \"no soliciting\" signs and gives up on a street that never ends.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using an exact in-memory HashSet for 5B URLs.</li>\n<li>Treating a Bloom filter \"yes\" as certain.</li>\n<li>Not normalising URLs before dedupe.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-interviewers-look-for","title":"What interviewers look for","html":"<ul>\n<li>A clear frontier with priority plus per-host politeness, and why partitioning by host works.</li>\n<li>URL and content dedupe with numbers (Bloom filter size, SimHash).</li>\n<li>Awareness of traps, robots.txt, timeouts and size caps.</li>\n<li>Sensible estimates: pages/s, bandwidth, storage per year, fetcher count.</li>\n<li>Fault tolerance via leases, at-least-once and idempotent writes.</li>\n<li>Freshness strategy beyond \"crawl everything again\".</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Crawl loop: frontier -> fetch -> parse -> dedupe -> back to frontier; store raw pages in a blob store.</li>\n<li>Frontier = priority front queues plus per-host back queues enforcing crawl-delay.</li>\n<li>Partition by host hash so politeness is local; this is hard to change later.</li>\n<li>Dedupe: normalise URLs, Bloom filter plus exact store; SHA-256 and SimHash for content.</li>\n<li>Defend against traps with depth, length, per-host budgets and body limits.</li>\n<li>Recrawl by estimated change rate using conditional GETs.</li>\n<li>~400 pages/s, ~1.6 Gbit/s, ~100 TB/month compressed for 1B pages/month.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}